--- a/spec/temdd/TEMDD_LANGUAGE_SPEC_V0_1.md
+++ b/spec/temdd/TEMDD_LANGUAGE_SPEC_V0_1.md
@@ -5,16 +5,31 @@ Status: executable bootstrap candidate. Authority: Goldkelch/qik-vrt.
 TEMDD (Tested Event Model Driven Development) is the executable metaprogramming language of QIK-VRT. Its lifecycle is `REQUEST -> EXECUTE -> FOLLOW -> LEARN -> SUCCESSOR -> ... -> DONE`.
 
 ## Normative invariants
-T01 Evidence is exact-subject typed and cannot transfer to another head/tree/scope. T02 Mutation creates a successor and invalidates dependent evidence. T03 TRANSPORT_ACK != EFFECT_ACK. T04 RESULT != EFFECT. T05 HOLD/CONTINUE are nonterminal and never NOOP. T06 Open productive work excludes DONE. T07 External effects require exact-scope authority. T08 Committed effects require fresh readback. T09 Missing/stale/conflicting/malformed/indeterminate critical evidence fails closed. T10 Unknown critical effect state blocks. T11 Learning constructs a successor and cannot self-certify. T12 DONE requires the complete declared DoD from fresh bound evidence.
+T01 Evidence is exact-subject typed and cannot transfer to another head/tree/scope.
+T02 Mutation creates a successor and invalidates dependent evidence.
+T03 TRANSPORT_ACK != EFFECT_ACK.
+T04 RESULT != EFFECT.
+T05 HOLD/CONTINUE are nonterminal and never NOOP.
+T06 Open productive work excludes DONE.
+T07 External effects require exact-scope authority.
+T08 Committed effects require fresh readback.
+T09 Missing/stale/conflicting/malformed/indeterminate critical evidence fails closed.
+T10 Unknown critical effect state blocks.
+T11 Learning constructs a successor and cannot self-certify.
+T12 DONE requires the complete declared DoD from fresh bound evidence.
+T13 Temporal provenance is two-dimensional: source order and local observation order are explicit and independent; emitted-at and observed-at are distinct fields. Observation order MUST NOT be rewritten into source order. A later local observation may legitimately reference an earlier source event; that classification never mutates past records.
+T14 Epistemic state is typed as TRUE, FALSE, UNKNOWN, CONFLICT, STALE, or UNOBSERVABLE. On the same exact subject and context, admissible learning may refine the knowledge region only by retaining or narrowing compatible states. CONFLICT, STALE, UNOBSERVABLE, and UNKNOWN cannot be coerced into TRUE, DONE, or EFFECT_ACK.
+T15 Context and perspective are first-class evidence bindings. A successor preserves the exact context/perspective or carries an explicitly authorized context transition; dependent predecessor evidence never transfers across context/perspective drift.
+T16 Representation is conservative. Canonical projections preserve every semantic field they claim to carry: authority, exact subject, context/perspective, relation endpoints and predicate, epistemic state, temporal provenance, and effect/readback obligations. Partial backends MUST declare their supported slice; omitted semantics confer no authority and cannot be inferred. Any disagreement is BLOCK.
 
 ## Semantic objects
-`authority`, `subject`, `request`, `event`, `test`, `evidence`, `model`, `effect`, `hold`, `learn`, `successor`, `done`. Models are not evidence. Effects have prepare/authorize/commit/readback boundaries.
+`authority`, `context`, `subject`, `relation`, `request`, `event`, `test`, `evidence`, `model`, `effect`, `hold`, `learn`, `successor`, `done`. Models are not evidence. Effects have prepare/authorize/commit/readback boundaries.
 
 ## Execution
 TEMDD is event-driven. Scheduling and polling are outer-layer transports, not kernel semantics. A runtime consumes one event, performs a finite transition, emits evidence/effect/successor intents and becomes quiescent. WAIT/HOLD, queued work, open PRs, unmerged productive branches, failed gates, missing releases and missing effect readback cannot become NOOP or DONE.
 
 ## Compilation
-`TEMDD source -> parser -> typed AST/IR -> conformance -> backend`. Initial backends are Python reference, Smalltalk live objects, C90 deterministic runtime, M68000 fixed relations and Lean obligations. Translators preserve subject identity, provenance, authority, status, effect state and readback obligations. Semantic loss or backend disagreement is BLOCK.
+`TEMDD source -> parser -> typed AST/IR -> conformance -> backend`. Initial backends are Python reference, Smalltalk live objects, C90 deterministic runtime, M68000 fixed relations and Lean obligations. Translators preserve subject identity, provenance, authority, status, context/perspective, relation identity, temporal ordering fields, effect state and readback obligations. A partial backend may carry a declared semantic slice only; semantic loss inside that slice or backend disagreement is BLOCK.
 
 ## Self-improvement
 `S --learn--> S'`. S' is a new exact subject. Evidence for S is not validation for S'. Fresh conformance and deployment evidence is mandatory before adoption.
@@ -26,7 +41,7 @@ TEMDD is event-driven. Scheduling and polling are outer-layer transports, not ke
 `ZERO_BUGS && ALL_PULL_REQUESTS_REGARDED && ALL_BRANCHES_REGARDED && ALL_PRODUCTIVE_BRANCHES_MERGED && FRESH_EXACT_MAIN_VALIDATION_PASS && FRESH_EFFECT_READBACK`.
 
 ## Bootstrap boundary
-v0.1 distinguishes BOOTSTRAP_CONFORMANT from STABLE_LANGUAGE. Stable status requires executable Smalltalk and M68000 gates, compiled Lean obligations, reproducible release, Main adoption and fresh production effect readback. Version labels and successful transport/build jobs cannot manufacture these claims. Intermediate states are observable but are not a return condition; the return condition is the full declared DoD.
+v0.1 distinguishes BOOTSTRAP_CONFORMANT from STABLE_LANGUAGE. T13-T16 are materialized as executable and formal candidate obligations, not as a production-effect claim. Stable status requires executable Smalltalk and M68000 gates, compiled Lean obligations, reproducible release, Main adoption and fresh production effect readback. Version labels and successful transport/build jobs cannot manufacture these claims. Intermediate states are observable but are not a return condition; the return condition is the full declared DoD.
 
 ## Conformance keywords
-MUST/MUST NOT define normative requirements; SHOULD is a strong recommendation overridable only with recorded evidence; MAY is optional. Any implementation claiming TEMDD v0.1 conformance MUST satisfy the executable positive/negative corpus and T01-T12 checks for the features it claims.
+MUST/MUST NOT define normative requirements; SHOULD is a strong recommendation overridable only with recorded evidence; MAY is optional. Any implementation claiming TEMDD v0.1 conformance MUST satisfy the executable positive/negative corpus and T01-T16 checks for the features it claims.
