-"SPDX-License-Identifier: PolyForm-Noncommercial-1.0.0"
-"Copyright 2026 Ingolf Lohmann. Verified snapshots, never network authority."
-Object subclass: #QikvrtEffectAck
-    instanceVariableNames: ''
-    classVariableNames: ''
-    package: 'QIKVRT-Core'!
-
-!QikvrtEffectAck class methodsFor: 'contract'!
-fields
-    ^ #(transport_ack input_identifier_available input_digest_valid
-        origin_checked context_checked semantics_reconstructed effect_anticipated
-        risk_classified risk_known responsibility_assigned responsibility_owner_present
-        connection_decided policy_allows_release deadline_exceeded no_open_questions
-        no_next_required_checks required_evidence_present predecessor_invalid integrity_failure)
-!
-stateNames
-    ^ #(EFFECT_NACK EFFECT_ACK_CONTINUE EFFECT_ACK_DONE EFFECT_ACK_ISOLATE EFFECT_ACK_BLOCK)
-!
-evaluate: snapshot
-    "Preserve the C90 verified-snapshot first-match order. Malformed snapshots block."
-    | decision complete |
-    (snapshot isKindOf: Dictionary) ifFalse: [ ^ #EFFECT_ACK_BLOCK ].
-    (self fields allSatisfy: [ :key |
-        (snapshot includesKey: key) and: [
-            (snapshot at: key) == true or: [ (snapshot at: key) == false ] ] ])
-        ifFalse: [ ^ #EFFECT_ACK_BLOCK ].
-    decision := snapshot at: #connection_decision ifAbsent: [ ^ #EFFECT_ACK_BLOCK ].
-    (decision isInteger and: [ decision between: 0 and: 4 ])
-        ifFalse: [ ^ #EFFECT_ACK_BLOCK ].
-    (snapshot at: #predecessor_invalid) ifTrue: [ ^ #EFFECT_ACK_BLOCK ].
-    (snapshot at: #deadline_exceeded) ifTrue: [ ^ #EFFECT_ACK_BLOCK ].
-    ((snapshot at: #input_identifier_available) and: [ snapshot at: #input_digest_valid ])
-        ifFalse: [ ^ #EFFECT_NACK ].
-    (snapshot at: #integrity_failure) ifTrue: [ ^ #EFFECT_ACK_BLOCK ].
-    decision = 4 ifTrue: [ ^ #EFFECT_ACK_BLOCK ].
-    decision = 3 ifTrue: [ ^ #EFFECT_ACK_ISOLATE ].
-    decision = 2 ifFalse: [ ^ #EFFECT_ACK_CONTINUE ].
-    complete := #(transport_ack input_digest_valid origin_checked context_checked
-        semantics_reconstructed effect_anticipated risk_classified risk_known
-        responsibility_assigned responsibility_owner_present connection_decided
-        policy_allows_release no_open_questions no_next_required_checks required_evidence_present)
-        allSatisfy: [ :key | snapshot at: key ].
-    ^ complete ifTrue: [ #EFFECT_ACK_DONE ] ifFalse: [ #EFFECT_ACK_CONTINUE ]
-!
-snapshotFromMask: mask decision: decision
-    | snapshot |
-    (mask isInteger and: [ mask between: 0 and: 524287 ])
-        ifFalse: [ self error: 'Snapshot mask outside 19-bit contract' ].
-    snapshot := Dictionary new.
-    self fields withIndexDo: [ :key :index |
-        snapshot at: key put: (mask bitAt: index) = 1 ].
-    snapshot at: #connection_decision put: decision.
-    ^ snapshot
-!
-coreCodeFor: state
-    ^ (self stateNames indexOf: state ifAbsent: [ ^ 4 ]) - 1
-!
-wireCodeFor: state
-    "D4 wire codes differ from the C enum. Never transmit the C index directly."
-    ^ #(0 1 4 2 3) at: (self coreCodeFor: state) + 1
-!
-ordinaryRelease: state
-    ^ state = #EFFECT_ACK_DONE
-! !
diff --git a/src/smalltalk/README.md b/src/smalltalk/README.md
deleted file mode 100644
index 335081828e21b11d91f2f712ae8a3d596d7b68fb..0000000000000000000000000000000000000000
--- a/src/smalltalk/README.md
+++ /dev/null
@@ -1,50 +0,0 @@
-# QIK-VRT Smalltalk core
-
-`QikvrtEffectAck.st` is an independently executable Pharo Smalltalk implementation
-of the C90 verified-snapshot kernel. Python remains the rich evidence/protocol
-adapter; C90 remains the dependency-minimal kernel. Existing Python functionality
-and tests are retained.
-
-The 19 Boolean fields and five decisions share the existing C90 test-mask order.
-All 2,621,440 combinations are compared byte-for-byte with the compiled C90
-kernel, whose existing suite independently checks 7,864,387 assertions. The
-Smalltalk test also rejects malformed snapshots and restores a freshly built
-image before testing. These counts refer to the stated domains, not to millions
-of independent end-to-end boot tests.
-
-Another 23 representable boundary cases compare the rich Python engine with
-the C90/Smalltalk results. Projection into the verified snapshot preserves
-Python's reception rule: without a transport acknowledgement, a raw identifier
-string is not an available effect-checkable input identity. This is a scoped
-adapter check, not a claim that every Python protocol feature was ported.
-
-```
-python3 -B tools/qikvrt_smalltalk.py install
-make smalltalk-test
-python3 -B tools/qikvrt_smalltalk.py build --output /tmp/qikvrt-smalltalk-image
-```
-
-Source is stored in Git as standard Smalltalk file-in text. The generated image
-is a derivative, not an editable source of authority. Each build begins with the
-locked upstream image and records the exact source, image and lock hashes. The
-Linux x86_64 VM and image archives are bound in `pharo-13.lock.json`; a changed
-upstream URL response fails closed. Rollback deletes only an incomplete new
-installation and never replaces a verified cache. A successful restore does not
-approve, publish, deploy or complete the broader project.
-
-The C enum and the Transputer D4 encoding are deliberately different:
-
-| State | C90 enum | D4 wire |
-| --- | ---: | ---: |
-| EFFECT_NACK | 0 | 0 |
-| EFFECT_ACK_CONTINUE | 1 | 1 |
-| EFFECT_ACK_DONE | 2 | 4 |
-| EFFECT_ACK_ISOLATE | 3 | 2 |
-| EFFECT_ACK_BLOCK | 4 | 3 |
-
-Use `wireCodeFor:` at the transport boundary; never send a C enum as D4 directly.
-
-Upstream: [Pharo download](https://pharo.org/download),
-[Pharo source](https://github.com/pharo-project/pharo),
-[VM source](https://github.com/pharo-project/pharo-vm).
-The upstream licenses are retained under `runtime/toolchains/pharo-*-LICENSE.txt`.
